31. Final Acceptance Criteria

The first release is complete only when:

A new user can register and verify an account.

The user can complete onboarding.

The user can select Germany as a destination and Master's study as a goal.

The system recommends relevant groups.

The user can join a public group.

The user can request access to a private group.

The user can publish and comment on posts.

The user can find another consenting member with a similar goal.

The user can send a permitted direct message.

A recipient can block and report abusive contact.

A moderator can review the report.

An administrator can manage groups and users.

Unauthorized users cannot access private groups, messages, or documents.

Data persists after refresh and server restart.

Automated critical-path tests pass.

The application can be deployed to a staging environment.

Start by generating the system architecture, database schema, application sitemap, design system, and implementation plan. Then build Phase 1 in small, testable modules.

Do not skip security, moderation, accessibility, or privacy requirements.

The final product should feel like a credible international community platform built specifically for Indian students, graduates, job seekers, and professionals preparing for opportunities abroad.